// Module 7 quiz - Deep Learning for AI Startups
$CATEGORY: $course$/Module 7

::M7 Q1:: What does RAG add to a language model? {
=Retrieved context from your documents#RAG looks up relevant passages first and gives them to the model, so it can answer from your data.
~More GPU memory
~A bigger vocabulary
~Automatic labeling
}

::M7 Q2:: Which step most limits answer quality in RAG? {
~Choosing the font of the UI
~The number of epochs
=Retrieving the right passages#If the right passage is not retrieved, the model cannot answer correctly, whatever the prompt says.
~Image augmentation
}

::M7 Q3:: How can you reduce hallucinations in a RAG prompt? {
~Ask it to be creative
~Remove the context
~Increase temperature
=Instruct the model to answer only from the context and admit when unsure#Grounding instructions, plus a clear way to say I don't know, keep the model from inventing answers.
}

::M7 Q4:: Why include citations? {
~They shorten prompts
=Users can verify answers and you can debug retrieval#A citation points to the passage behind the answer, so people can check it and you can see what retrieval found.
~They train the model
~They hide errors
}

::M7 Q5:: What mainly drives per-request cost in RAG? {
=Tokens sent and generated#You pay for tokens in and out, and the retrieved passages make up most of the tokens sent.
~Screen resolution
~Number of users logged in
~The programming language
}
